% jfb 1
$$\int \frac{\text{d} x}{x} = \ln |x| + C$$
---

# $\Gamma _0 = \alpha _0: x \in \mathbb{R}$

$[\mathbb{R}::\text{div}]$
$x < 0 \to \square\ \alpha _1$
$x = 0 \to \blacksquare$
$x > 0 \to \square\ \alpha _2$
---

## $\Gamma _0 \to \Gamma _1 = \alpha _1: x < 0$

$$\ln |x| = \ln (- x)$$

$\frac{\text{d} \ln {\color{Peach} |x|}}{\text{d} x}$
$= \frac{\text{d} \ln (- x)}{\text{d} x}$
$= {\color{Peach} \frac{\text{d} \ln (- x)}{\text{d} (- x)}} \cdot {\color{Peach} \frac{\text{d} (- x)}{\text{d} x}}$
$= {\color{Peach} -} \frac{1}{x} \cdot {\color{Peach} (- 1)}$
$= \frac{1}{x}$

$\blacksquare\ \alpha _1$
---

## $\Gamma _0 \to \Gamma _2 = \alpha _2: x > 0$

$$\ln |x| = \ln x$$

$\frac{\text{d} \ln {\color{Peach} |x|}}{\text{d} x}$
$= {\color{Peach} \frac{\text{d} \ln x}{\text{d} x}}$
$= \frac{1}{x}$

$\blacksquare\ \alpha _2$

## $\Gamma _0 = \Gamma _1 + \Gamma _2$

$$\frac{\text{d} \ln |x|}{\text{d} x} = \frac{1}{x} \quad (x \ne 0)$$

$[\mathbb{R}::\text{int}]$
$\mathbf{ori}\ C \in \mathbb{R}$

$$\int \frac{\text{d} x}{x} = \ln |x| + {\color{Cyan} C} \quad (x \ne 0, {\color{Cyan} C} \in \mathbb{R})$$

$\blacksquare\ \alpha _0$
